---
description: Split a file that outgrows one responsibility into a folder
alwaysApply: true
---

# Split large files

One responsibility per file. Start from these modules:

- `src/main.ts` wires the page
- `src/firebase.ts` sets up the client
- `src/auth.ts` signs in and requires a verified email
- `src/person.ts` stores legal name, WhatsApp, email, emergency contact, and the ticket checkbox
- `src/accommodations.ts` stores RV, trailer, yurt, and shiftpod rows, with length, width, and occupants
- `src/vehicles.ts` stores driven vehicles, with length, width, and a vehicle pass
- `src/availability.ts` stores early build and late teardown
- `src/roles.ts` stores willingness to lead and to contribute
- `src/admin.ts` stores the one appointed lead per role

An RV's vehicle pass stays on the accommodation. A trailer has none. The tow vehicle is a vehicle. Occupants are registered accounts.

Split a file in the same change when it takes a second responsibility or passes about 200 lines. Move the pieces into a folder named for that responsibility. `index.ts` re-exports the public functions and types, and other modules keep importing the folder.

```
src/accommodations.ts
```

becomes

```
src/accommodations/index.ts
src/accommodations/types.ts
src/accommodations/footprint.ts
src/accommodations/occupants.ts
src/accommodations/occupants.test.ts
```

Tests move with the code they cover. `index.ts` only re-exports.
